            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i244KY80OGQTMbnJU"
              ><h3><strong>The Hijacked Reflex</strong></h3></div
            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iY6RQVP4Y8TqxFAZ9"
              ><p>The problem is that in the modern world, we’ve hijacked this primitive reflex. We’ve attached it to toxic habits, vapes, cigarettes, endless caffeine, or processed sugar, just to get that 5-second feeling of "relief."</p><p></p><p>We’ve been conditioned to believe we are addicted to the <strong>chemicals.</strong> But for most of us, we are actually addicted to the <strong>motion.</strong> We don&apos;t want the nicotine. We don&apos;t want the "burnt popcorn" smell of a vape. We don&apos;t even really want the sugar crash.</p><p></p><p><strong>We want the pause.</strong> We want that tiny, 5-second window where the world stops, our breath deepens, and our hands have a "job" to do.</p></div
            ></div
          ></div
        ></div
